on model. For Carol choice c, the winning events A<c<B and B<c<A are disjoint. For 1/2<=c<=2/3 the probability is c*(4-6*c)+(1-c)*(6*c-3)=25/48-12*(c-13/24)^2. For 0<=c<=1/2 it is c; for 2/3<=c<=1 it is 1-c. The interior maximizer c=13/24 has value 25/48>1/2, greater than every outer-piece value, so B. Preserve H-approved geometric probability with all three optional quadratic-vertex, square-completion and polynomial-derivative routes. Only the middle quadratic is differentiated, and the outer intervals are checked. Uniform marginal distributions alone do not imply independence; retain that ordinary model qualification with normal grading rather than silently converting it into a confirmed defect.","recordedAnswer":"B","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h222"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":["The calculation uses the usual interpretation that Alice's and Bob's random choices are independent.","independent_player_randomization_convention_explicit","Independence of Alice's and Bob's choices is the conventional interpretation used here. Their marginal uniform distributions alone do not determine Carol's winning probability."],"questionId":"2018_AMC_12A_Q24","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"polynomial-derivative","label":"Differentiate only the polynomial middle piece","methodDirectNodeIds":{"polynomial-derivative":["cnm_h222","cnm_h226","cnm_h227"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h222","cnm_h226","cnm_h227"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"alignmentIds":["alignment:2b8e8b2b27e922b8c975a91e"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"2","reason":"f'(x)=2x-4, and 2x-4=0 gives x=2.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_h222"],"coverage":"aligned_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_h225_q1","reviewStatus":"machine_adjudicated","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_097","cnm_h032"],"id":"differentiate-and-solve","label":"Differentiate and solve","methodDirectNod